{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865528-how-can-i-send-a-player-off-awesomely","id":865528,"title":"How can I send a player off awesomely?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-14T08:55:45-07:00","id":865528,"title":"How can I send a player off awesomely?","content":"I've got a player who accepted a job in another state. He leaves in a few weeks, and told me he's got two more sessions of Vampire with us. It's a sad day, but there you go.<br /> <br /> I want to make the next two sessions <i>awesome</i>. He's relatively new to Vampire, though he's vaguely aware of it as a long-time gamer. Some details:<br /> <br /> He's playing a Daeva member of the Weihan Cynn (Requiem for Regina). His requests for stuff coming up:<br /> <br /> 1) I think I'd like to see how we fare up against things other than humans in combat.<br /> 2) I'd like to meet/deal with some of the supers of Britain outside of just the stuff in the city of London.<br /> 3) I'd also like to do something very Vampire-y, but I'm not sure what that is. Or even what I'm looking for.<br /> <br /> On elaborating about 3), he said, &quot;I feel that the human brain and feelings/conscience inside the player is interfering with some of getting into the character.&quot; I told him that was sort of by design since humanity vs monstrosity is a big theme of Vampire, but I'm going to try to take it into consideration anyway.<br /> <br /> After looking at the sidebar about the other supernatural creatures of the era, one thing that looks interesting is &quot;Wolf-blooded have recently been going through the First Change with much greater frequency than usual.&quot; I figure if a werewolf awakens in their territory, it gives them all sorts of potential things to do for a whole session, if not more: they have to find the werewolf, subdue them, if they don't kill them then figure out what to do with them. &quot;Donating&quot; a freshly-changed werewolf to one of the packs outside of the city may be the sort of thing that gives an aspiring Weihan Cynn member some good contacts with the local Uratha.<br /> <br /> Our sessions are on Mondays, and I'll post updates and ideas that I've got. Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T09:18:22-07:00","id":865539,"title":"","content":"For point 3, it sounds like the player wants his character to do something really extreme, but has trouble bringing himself to do it, due to his own sense of ethics as a player. Have you considered asking him for permission to temporarily take control of his character away from him, and have him do something &quot;vampire-y&quot; during that loss of control?<br /> <br /> For example, you could try taking a leaf from the Werewolf Storyelling chapter and have him black out during a frenzy and find when he comes to that someone or something important to him is dead or destroyed by his own hands (agreed upon ahead of time or chosen from a list of characters and things he's ok with losing to such a plot event).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe you could capitalize on his feelings that his own moral center is getting in the way of allowing the character to do truly &quot;vampire-y&quot; things by roleplaying the internal struggle between his human consciousness (played by him) and his Beast, or maybe an external influence like a possessing Strix (played by you or another player). Introduce some sort of mechanic to determine which force is in control of the character at any given moment, and have the malevolent force do &quot;vampire-y&quot; things while it is in control.<br /> <br /> You could even combine these two ideas, having the who's-in-control mechanic be the determining factor for when blackouts start. Either way though, these suggestions do require the player to sacrifice control of the character, and it's possible he won't find the &quot;vampire-y&quot; things the character does as meaningful if he doesn't have agency over them. So definitely ask if he feels like this sort of thing might satisfy that itch for him before making any more specific plans about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-14-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T09:59:26-07:00","id":865561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865528-how-can-i-send-a-player-off-awesomely#post865528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking at the sidebar about the other supernatural creatures of the era, one thing that looks interesting is &quot;Wolf-blooded have recently been going through the First Change with much greater frequency than usual.&quot; I figure if a werewolf awakens in their territory, it gives them all sorts of potential things to do for a whole session, if not more: they have to find the werewolf, subdue them, if they don't kill them then figure out what to do with them. &quot;Donating&quot; a freshly-changed werewolf to one of the packs outside of the city may be the sort of thing that gives an aspiring Weihan Cynn member some good contacts with the local Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your PC feed on humans? If so, I think I would suggest that the PC is on a typical feeding run, and the feeding actually triggers the First Change in his victim. I would play up two things - trying to make the PC feel responsible for event, but also encouraging the PC to feel sympathetic toward the werewolf, seeing someone thrust into the realm of frenzy / beast. Maybe the victim even manages to get out, &quot;Help me... I don't know what's happening...&quot; before the change takes over fully.<br /> <br /> (Sidebar - I haven't read Werewolf since the Apocalypse, so I don't know how much of this would be still kosher in terms of First Changes triggered by trauma).<br /> <br /> I'd try and put the whole thing in a situation where the beast running rampant causes some consequences to maybe Feeding Grounds or special locations, something that gives a little sting to letting this new wolf run rampant, but that isn't an automatic - <i>we need to put this thing down </i>decision. Take the Masquerade off the table, but make it personally inconvenient to the PC or their agendas. Hopefully, the PC attempts to subdue the beast, and now you have that cross-splat fight.<br /> <br /> I'd also give the PC a new condition to represent feeding on the blood of a pre/currently changing werewolf. The blood runs hot, thick with hormones, etc. Tailor the condition to specifically counter what you glean the player is holding back. &quot;Gain a beat whenever you react out of primal aggression&quot; &quot;Gain a beat whenever you act quickly instead of logically&quot; - I know the player didn't give a lot of details on what's holding them back, but I'd take my best guess.<br /> <br /> If there have been any past scenes where this PC frenzied in way that bit them in the butt hard, I'd try and incorporate that past scene into this one, maybe allowing the PC to think &quot;I'm not gonna let this happen to someone else&quot; or &quot;I can do better this time&quot; - give them some catharsis as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 04-14-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:21:21-07:00","id":865612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865528-how-can-i-send-a-player-off-awesomely?p=865561#post865561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sidebar - I haven't read Werewolf since the Apocalypse, so I don't know how much of this would be still kosher in terms of First Changes triggered by trauma).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely still a thing in Forsaken, 2e even has optional rules for tracking rising tension that could erupt into a Fitst Change if you want to start out play as a Wolf Blooded and change in-game.<br /> <br /> Also, awesome idea, kind of blows my suggestion out of the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:47:58-07:00","id":865630,"title":"","content":"If you had more time, I would try something very radical - basically, a character discovers after a slight time jump that their memories were modified by Domination. Obviously, players would want to investigate and get their memories back. Investigation ensues, and it starts to uncover some really disturbing stuff; something bestial and inherently inhuman. For added creepy factor, include random flickers of modified memories, flickers that are full of really unpleasant and scary emotions, something out of horror, something bestial. Show some consequences of that bestial thing, in general make your player think about it for a bit.<br /> In the end, let them find the dude who Dominated them (I say them, but I mean that player specifically), and demand to fix his charm. With some sighing and &quot;I don't want to do this, and you really don't want it either, but you are forcing my hand&quot;, he does it. Your player should probably have very uncomfortable gut feeling about what is coming next. Because what comes next is, well, remembering that it was *you* who did that Horrible Monster Thing, and you regretted it a lot, and that Vampire Dominated it out of your head because you asked for it / because he felt like you would otherwise totally lose yourself. <br /> <br /> Properly executed, such story should be chilly and creepy, and invite a lot of questions about how little it takes for a person to turn into a monster; it would be also good to make sure that while even before the reveal, the crime is monstrous, but also somewhat, chillingly, understandable. Still, something like this takes a lot of time, preparation, and you need to really understand your player to pull it off (and, obviously, they must be a type of people who would enjoy such a story); definitely not for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T12:00:41-07:00","id":865640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865528-how-can-i-send-a-player-off-awesomely?p=865630#post865630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you had more time, I would try something very radical - basically, a character discovers after a slight time jump that their memories were modified by Domination. Obviously, players would want to investigate and get their memories back. Investigation ensues, and it starts to uncover some really disturbing stuff; something bestial and inherently inhuman. For added creepy factor, include random flickers of modified memories, flickers that are full of really unpleasant and scary emotions, something out of horror, something bestial. Show some consequences of that bestial thing, in general make your player think about it for a bit.<br /> In the end, let them find the dude who Dominated them (I say them, but I mean that player specifically), and demand to fix his charm. With some sighing and &quot;I don't want to do this, and you really don't want it either, but you are forcing my hand&quot;, he does it. Your player should probably have very uncomfortable gut feeling about what is coming next. Because what comes next is, well, remembering that it was *you* who did that Horrible Monster Thing, and you regretted it a lot, and that Vampire Dominated it out of your head because you asked for it / because he felt like you would otherwise totally lose yourself.<br /> <br /> Properly executed, such story should be chilly and creepy, and invite a lot of questions about how little it takes for a person to turn into a monster; it would be also good to make sure that while even before the reveal, the crime is monstrous, but also somewhat, chillingly, understandable. Still, something like this takes a lot of time, preparation, and you need to really understand your player to pull it off (and, obviously, they must be a type of people who would enjoy such a story); definitely not for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well shit, I'm at least keeping this idea for the rest of the group. Especially given the number of spineless, ruthless, monster Ventrue the players came up with during Climbing the Ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T13:05:26-07:00","id":865664,"title":"","content":"Considering that Player will no longer be able to play, you would also be retiring their character. The question is - how? This is the occasion to stop playing conservatively. The events of these two sessions can lead to any of the following:<br /> <br /> Heroic death when battling a strange foe, or defending what matters to them.<br /> Upsetting the order of the city and fleeing the consequences.<br /> Earning glory and leaving as emissary to other Beings.<br /> Seclusion, degeneration or insanity.<br /> Betraying other players.<br /> <br /> Try to recall what was the Vampire's character arc and what made them tick. Incorporate it into the story. Use Fiasco RPG rules if you need to. If the rest of the group are willing to deal with the fallout - all the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T15:47:33-07:00","id":865727,"title":"","content":"To add one more option:<br /> <br /> A sudden backstabbing death. But done in such a way that they get the last laugh, as (for example, borrowing from <b>L.A. Confidential</b>) they get to leave the conspirators misinformed and the other PCs clued in by their last words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T15:55:45-07:00","id":865730,"title":"","content":"You know what's very Vampirey? Embracing someone. Did they have a chance do it? Another classic story is one where you think that you have to power about another's life and turn them into something monstrous, and then have to deal with consequences, often ending in a death of the creator at the hands of their child. Even without the parentcide, it's a very interesting experience, one deeply rooted in the vampire state.<br /> And if their heir does something, you can banish them from London, due to being responsible from their childes actions, so you don't have to kill the character while putting it on a bus.<br /> Another thing worth experiencing is Diablerie. Either diablerizing someone (combine that with the Dominate Erased Memory story...) or being diablerized yourself. Or, if you want to make it bittersweet, start the game with the scene of your player being diablerized, then go &quot;back a few nights&quot;, tell the story about how it happened, and let other player possibly save the guy in the last moment, but leaving him with heavily damaged soul; damaged enough so only way to save them is to put them into torpor and safeguarding for few next decades.<br /> Actually, you could make it a story about other supernatural splat &quot;diablerizing&quot; a Vampire.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Other thing I've always wanted to try was a Reverse Diablerie story. Basically, someone tried to eat your soul, and for whatever reason, it backfired and instead of being devoured, you were the one who survived, while the other dude...yeah. I want to do this next time I can play Vampire, as a starting Persistent Condition (I find perspective of very young Vampire, who probably was Embraced only to get eaten by her Sire, accidentally doing this in her first hour of unlife, and then suffering from the stigma for the rest of her Requiem), I totally can see this as an exit story, where again, you survive, but get banished out of the community.<br /> <br /> EDIT2<br /> I don't remember all the relevant rules, but one of most traumatic things you could inflict upon a vampire, would be being possesed by a Strix who in turn proceeds to diablerize someone while riding in your body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-14-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T18:54:40-07:00","id":865776,"title":"","content":"Have him ride a shark covered in explosives into a volcano, thereby wiping out a small island nation.<br /> <br /> I say this without having read the thread. I just assume it will be appropriate for now and will re-evalutate it after I read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T22:29:29-07:00","id":865811,"title":"","content":"Have a strange new big and bad from outside invade their territory in a loud and violent way. The players hunt it down, confronting it on this player's last session, turning into a violent fight while in a frenzy (holding nothing back, like a true monster). Arrange for the player's character to die while taking his enemy with him. He gets a 'heroic' end for his character while finally getting to unleash the beast without fear of consequences or an attack of conscience. Then after that player is gone the remaining members of the group learn that the big bad was just the frontrunner for something worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T00:18:54-07:00","id":865834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/865528-how-can-i-send-a-player-off-awesomely?p=865776#post865776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have him ride a shark covered in explosives into a volcano, thereby wiping out a small island nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came here to suggest &quot;set adrift in a blazing longboat&quot;, but I like yours better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T07:34:20-07:00","id":865938,"title":"","content":"I was reading through the Changeling stuff in Requiem for Regina, when suddenly something clicked: The PC's Touchstone is an 11-year old orphan (his fault) named Jane. And he wants to involve himself in faerie-related stuff, including combat with other supernatural creatures. Methinks an abduction is in the works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}